id: pm-web-vyxu
title: Adopt canonical proofs for shell aliases and publisher argument forwarding
description: "Move the supplemental public-package attestation rejection rules and adversarial corpus into pm-ops, publish the canonical auditor, then update the exact consumer pin and remove the boundary only when the corpus passes through the canonical export. Scope includes aliases, partially expanded executable names, forwarded publisher subcommands, executable arrays, quoted executable word boundaries, unknown flags and independent workflow run scopes. This follow-up does not authorize changes to another repository during the current package task."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T21:01:47.193Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T21:27:16.727Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:02:35.506Z",codex-sol,"Canonical work required: pm-ops 2026.10.4 silently accepts an enabled npm-publish alias, npm \"$@\" function forwarding, a partially expanded executable such as n$(printf pm), and provenance scalar evidence shared across separate workflow run steps. The consumer guard adds failures using the canonical scanner, with actual run bodies parsed independently. Known additional canonical noise: a workflow step name containing eval \"$UNKNOWN\" is scanned as shell and can cause a false rejection; the consumer preserves canonical failures rather than overriding them. Carry the adversarial corpus upstream and address workflow executable-data boundaries before removing this guard."
  "2026-10-07T21:27:16.727Z",codex-sol,"Expanded canonical corpus includes combined variable/function indirection: ship() { NPM=npm; $NPM \"$@\"; } hides publishing from the pinned auditor. Variables resolving to alias, eval and builtin eval also hide alias-created publishing. The consumer rejects unknown arguments on variable-routed commands and variable-routed aliases/evaluators using canonical tokenization of literal leading bindings as rejection evidence only. A literal npm dist-tag named eval and a literal array-looking argument remain accepted controls."
